<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>SubgenAI.SerenityStar.SDK</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>SerenityStar</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>SerenityStar</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Official .NET SDK for Serenity Star API: agents (assistants, copilots, activities, AI proxies and chat completions). AI services are available in SubgenAI.SerenityStar.AIServices.</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>ai;chat;sdk;serenity;serenitystar</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
      Version 3.0.0-beta2 - Package Split Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Skill Approvals: agents pause when a skill that requires approval is invoked, and the SDK can now answer them
        * New ApprovalPendingAction ("approval") in AgentResult.PendingActions with RequestId, CallId, SkillCode, SkillType, Tool and Arguments
        * ApprovalPendingAction.Approve(reason) / Reject(reason) create the ApprovalDecision to send back
        * Assistants and Copilots: conversation.SendApprovalsAsync(decisions, message) and StreamApprovalsAsync(decisions, message)
          answer the pending approvals and continue the execution
        * AI Proxy: ProxyExecutionReq.AddApprovalDecision(approval, decision) echoes the request and the decision in the
          client-side history (ProxyExecutionMessage.ToolApprovalRequest / ToolApprovalResponse)
        * AI Proxy skills: ProxyExecutionReq.Skills enables web search, image generation, speech generation and workbench
          per request, each with its own RequiresApproval setting
        * Streaming: StreamingAgentMessageTaskStop.TryGetApprovalRequest surfaces the approval as soon as it is requested,
          and StreamingTaskKeys exposes the approval task keys
        * Unanswered approvals: StreamingAgentMessageError.PendingActions and SerenityApiException.GetPendingActions()
          return the approvals still pending
        * Auto mode: AgentExecutionReq.Skills = new SkillsOptions { AutoMode = true } approves every skill invocation
          without pausing (Assistants and Copilots). Opt-in only: it bypasses the human review
      - Request User Choice: agents with the skill enabled pause to ask the user to choose from a set of options, and the
        SDK can now answer them
        * New UserChoicePendingAction ("user_choice") in AgentResult.PendingActions with its Questions (Id, Header, Text,
          IsMultiselect and Options with Id, Title and Description)
        * UserChoiceQuestion.Select(optionIds), AnswerOther(text) and Answer(optionIds, text) create a UserChoiceAnswer
          validated against the question
        * Assistants and Copilots: conversation.SendUserChoicesAsync(answers, message) and StreamUserChoicesAsync(answers, message)
          answer all, some or none of the questions and continue the conversation
        * AI Proxy: ProxySkillsOptions.UserChoice enables the skill per request, and
          ProxyExecutionReq.AddUserChoiceAnswers(userChoice, answers, message) echoes the questions and the answers in the
          client-side history (ProxyExecutionMessage.UserChoiceRequest / UserChoiceResponse)
        * Streaming: StreamingAgentMessageTaskStop.TryGetUserChoiceRequest surfaces the questions as soon as they are
          asked, and StreamingTaskKeys.UserChoiceRequest exposes its task key
      - Agent TODOs: agents with the skill enabled plan their own TODO list and keep iterating until it is done, and the
        SDK now exposes its progress while streaming (Assistants and Copilots)
        * StreamingAgentMessageTaskStop.TryGetAgentTodos returns the whole list (AgentTodoItem with Id, Description and
          Status) from the TODO skill tasks and the agent iteration task
        * AgentTodoStatus exposes the known statuses (Pending, Completed, Canceled), and StreamingTaskKeys.AgentTodoIterate
          the iteration task key

      FIXES:
      - Pending actions are now resolved by their "type": responses with pending actions no longer fail to deserialize,
        and unknown pending action types are surfaced as UnsupportedPendingAction instead of failing
      - "user_choice" pending actions are now surfaced as UserChoicePendingAction instead of UnsupportedPendingAction

      BREAKING CHANGES:
      - The SDK is now split into packages that are always published together with the same version:
        * SubgenAI.SerenityStar.Core: SerenityClient, SerenityClientBuilder, SerenityApiException and AddSerenityStar
        * SubgenAI.SerenityStar.SDK (this package): agents. Depends on Core
        * SubgenAI.SerenityStar.AIServices: all AI services. Depends on Core only:
          anonymizer, decisions, embeddings, image generation, OCR, speech generation and transcription
        Namespaces are unchanged, so most code only needs the new entry points below.
      - Agents are now obtained from SerenityClient: client.Agents becomes client.GetAgents()
        (in the SerenityStar.Client namespace). e.g. client.GetAgents().Activities.Create("agent-code")
      - ISerenityClient was removed. Inject SerenityClient (registered by AddSerenityStar), or AgentsScope after
        calling services.AddSerenityStar(apiKey).AddSerenityStarAgents()
      - client.AIServices (transcription) was removed from this package. Install SubgenAI.SerenityStar.AIServices
        and use client.GetTranscriptionClient().TranscribeAsync(...)

      Version 3.0.0-beta1 - Per-Request Authentication Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Richer error information: failed API responses now throw SerenityApiException (in the
        SerenityStar.Exceptions namespace) exposing StatusCode, ReasonPhrase and the parsed JSON error
        payload as ResponseJson (a JsonElement?, null for non-JSON bodies such as HTTP 429).
        It derives from HttpRequestException, so existing catch (HttpRequestException) handlers keep working.

      BREAKING CHANGES:
      - Authentication is now attached per-request instead of on HttpClient.DefaultRequestHeaders.
        A caller-provided HttpClient (via SerenityClientBuilder.WithHttpClient) is no longer mutated:
        its BaseAddress, Timeout and default headers are left untouched, and the API key is applied
        to each outgoing request. Configure the timeout on your own client; SerenityClientBuilder.WithTimeout
        is ignored when a custom HttpClient is supplied.
      - Direct construction entry points that took a raw HttpClient are no longer public. Create agents
        through SerenityClient (e.g. client.Agents.Activities.Create(...)) instead:
        * Activity, ChatCompletion and Proxy constructors are now internal
        * Conversation.CreateConversation(HttpClient, ...) is now internal
        * SystemAgentBase and ConversationalAgentBase base constructors are now internal
        * SerenityClient's internal builder constructor now takes a SerenityApiClient

      Version 2.5.0 - Streaming Events Enhancement Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Reasoning Events: New StreamingAgentMessageReasoning ("reasoning") surfaces model reasoning text during streaming

      - Ping Events: New StreamingAgentMessagePing ("ping") represents keep-alive pings sent during streaming

      - Citations: Content events (StreamingAgentMessageContent) now expose a Citations list linking response spans back to their source
        * CitationResult carries CitationIndex, StartIndex/EndIndex, Relevance, CitedText, and Source metadata
        * Polymorphic SourceInfo resolved by "type": KnowledgeFile, KnowledgeWebsite, and WebSearch

      - Forward-Compatible Unsupported Events: Unknown streaming message types are now surfaced as StreamingAgentMessageUnsupported (with OriginalType and the raw JSON payload) instead of failing the stream with an error

      IMPROVEMENTS:
      - Task Events: StreamingAgentMessageTaskStart now includes Metadata, and StreamingAgentMessageTaskStop now includes a Success flag


      Version 2.4.0 - Message Feedback Comments Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Feedback Comments: SubmitFeedbackReq now accepts an optional Comment explaining why a message was rated that way
        * Limited to 1000 characters by the API, which rejects longer values with an HTTP 400 response
        * Blank comments are stored as no comment, and re-submitting feedback overwrites the previously stored comment

      - Message Feedback Retrieval: Audit the feedback submitted for a conversational agent
        * GetMessageFeedbackAsync(agentCode, GetMessageFeedbackReq) on Assistants and Copilots - Page through the feedback submitted for an agent, including comments
        * Supports paging (page size capped at 1000), date range filtering and sort direction
        * Requires an API key with the Audit permission for the agent, and returns end-user conversation content and user identifiers
        * Feedback is tied to a conversation message, so it is not available for Activities, Chat Completions or AI Proxies

      Version 2.3.0 - Agent-Scoped Volatile Knowledge Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Agent-Scoped Volatile Knowledge Upload: Upload volatile knowledge validated against an agent's configured allowed MIME types at upload time
        * UploadForAgentAsync(UploadVolatileKnowledgeReq) - Upload a file or content scoped to the agent
        * UploadFromFileForAgentAsync(UploadVolatileKnowledgeFromFileReq) - Upload from an existing file ID
        * UploadFromUrlForAgentAsync(UploadVolatileKnowledgeFromUrlReq) - Upload from a URL
        * UploadFromBase64ForAgentAsync(UploadVolatileKnowledgeFromBase64Req) - Upload from base64-encoded content
        * GetAllowedMimeTypesAsync() - Retrieve the MIME types allowed for the agent (falls back to all platform-supported types when none are configured)

      - Volatile Knowledge Metadata: VolatileKnowledgeRes now exposes FileId, EmbeddingsGenerated, and Scanned

      IMPROVEMENTS:
      - The existing subtenant-scoped UploadAsync remains available for uploads without agent-level MIME type validation

      Version 2.2.0 - Transcription and Audio Input Release

      NEW FEATURES:
      - AI Services Scope: New top-level AIServices scope for accessing AI-powered services
        * client.AIServices.Transcription for audio/video transcription

      - Audio Transcription:
        * TranscribeAsync(TranscribeAudioReq) - Upload and transcribe audio/video files directly
        * Supported formats: mp3, mp4, mpeg, mpga, m4a, wav, webm (max 25 MB)
        * Returns transcript text, metadata, token usage, and cost
        * Optional model selection, prompt guidance, user tracking, and channel

      - Agent Audio Input: Send audio file streams to agents for automatic upload, transcription and processing
        * Conversational agents (Assistants/Copilots): Pass audioStream and audioFileName to SendMessageAsync or StreamMessageAsync
        * Activity agents: Set AudioFileStream and AudioFileName on AgentExecutionReq
        * Chat Completion agents: Set AudioFileStream and AudioFileName on ChatCompletionReq
        * message and audioStream are mutually exclusive — providing both throws ArgumentException

      IMPROVEMENTS:
      - ChatCompletionReq.Message is now nullable (string?) to support audio-only requests
      - ChatCompletionReq.Validate() method for mutual exclusion validation
      - Conversation.SendMessageAsync and StreamMessageAsync: new overloads accepting (Stream audioStream, string audioFileName) for audio input

      Version 2.1.0 - API Enhancement Release

      IMPROVEMENTS:
      - Agent Version Management: Simplified agent version specification
        * Pass optional agent version directly as method parameters instead of using AgentVersion property
        * Activities.Create(agentCode, version, options)
        * Assistants.CreateConversation(agentCode, version, options)
        * ChatCompletions.Create(agentCode, version, options)
        * GetInfoByCodeAsync(agentCode, version, options) support for versioned agent info retrieval

      - API Refactoring: Cleaner and more intuitive method signatures
        * Removed AgentVersion property from ChatCompletionReq and AgentExecutionReq
        * Version parameter is now consistently passed at creation time
        * Improved method overloads for better discoverability

      - Code Quality:
        * Better separation of concerns in version handling
        * Consistent parameter ordering across all agent types
        * Enhanced XML documentation for clarity

      Version 2.0.1 - Hotfix
      - Fixed GuardrailRuleViolation.Rule property type from string to int to match API response
      - Simplified GuardrailRuleViolation constructors removing automatic RuleName assignment

      Version 2.0.0 - Major Release

      BREAKING CHANGES:
      - Renamed SerenityAIHubClient to SerenityClient
      - Complete API redesign to provide scoped methods based on agent types and other core entities (e.g., client.Agents.Activities.ExecuteAsync("agent-name"), conversation.SendMessageAsync("message"))

      NEW FEATURES:
      - Builder Pattern for Client Creation:
        * SerenityClientBuilder with fluent API for flexible configuration
        * Support for custom HttpClient injection
        * Configurable timeouts and base URLs

      - Volatile Knowledge Management: Upload and manage temporary documents (files or text) that can be used in agent executions with expiration control
        * client.Agents.VolatileKnowledge.UploadAsync() - Upload documents or text content
        * client.Agents.VolatileKnowledge.GetStatusAsync() - Check processing status
        * Support for embeddings processing, custom expiration dates, and callback URLs
        * Use volatile knowledge IDs in agent executions for context-aware responses

      - Enhanced Connector Support: Better integration with external services
        * conversation.GetConnectorStatusAsync(connectorId) - Check connection status for external services
        * Support for ConnectionPendingAction with connector details (ConnectorId, Url, ConnectorName, ConnectorImgUrl)
        * Improved handling of pending actions requiring user authentication
        * Support for connector authentication workflows in conversations

      - Unified Streaming Experience: Consistent streaming across all agent types
        * Activities: activity.StreamAsync()
        * Chat Completions: chatCompletion.StreamAsync()
        * AI Proxy: proxy.StreamAsync()
        * Assistants: conversation.StreamMessageAsync()
        * Receive real-time updates with start, content, task logs, and stop events

      IMPROVEMENTS:
      - Enhanced error handling with detailed HTTP error messages
      - Improved XML documentation across all public APIs
      - Better type safety and null handling
      - Consistent parameter naming and structure

      DOCUMENTATION:
      - Updated execution examples for all agents
      - Streaming examples for each agent type
      - Step-by-step guides for volatile knowledge workflows
      - Connector integration patterns
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SerenityStar.Core\SerenityStar.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>